                      "regime": "$regime",
                      "band": "$band",
                      "resident": "$resident",
                      "status": "$status",
                      "lottery": "$lottery",
                      "online_games": "$online_games",
                      "vda": "$vda",
                      "agri": "$agri",
                      "excess_112": "$excess_112"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "returns": "record",
  "version": 5,
  "status": "published",
  "description_nl": "2026-10-06: slab tax on normal income (old regime by age; new the same for all), 111A at 20% and 112A at 12.5% above 1.25 lakh, 112 at 12.5%; a resident's unused basic exemption first eats into those gains; 87A (resident, total up to 12 lakh new / 5 lakh old) - in the new regime only against normal-rate tax, with marginal relief just above 12 lakh; surcharge on the tax (special gains at most 15%) with marginal relief; 4% cess; tax rounded to the nearest 10 (288B). 2026-10-06: status - the 87A rebate and its marginal relief are for a resident individual only (an HUF pays tax on 12 lakh). 2026-10-07: special-rate income: 115BB (lottery, crossword, races, card games, gambling, betting), 115BBJ (online games) and 115BBH (virtual digital assets) at 30% each, in both regimes - no basic exemption against them, no 87A rebate on their tax (they still count in total income for the 87A limit), surcharge on them at the full rate (the 15% cap is for 111A / 112 / 112A only). Agricultural income above 5,000 with total income above the basic exemption: partial integration in both regimes - tax on (normal + agri) less tax on (basic exemption + agri); on_aggregate / agri_rebate are the two figures Part B-TTI shows. 2026-10-07: excess_112: for land / building bought before 23 July 2024 (resident), the tax at 12.5% without indexation less the tax at 20% with it is left out of the 112 tax (never below nil) - surcharge and cess are on what is left. 2026-10-10: the same expressions in stages (chips myreturn.tax_s1 - s5, each reading what the stage before worked out) instead of every field holding a copy of the fields it needs - 1.18 MB on disk to a few dozen KB; answers checked identical on the chip's cases and 6,000 random returns (tools/slim_myreturn_tax.py), about three times faster.",
